        "id": 185604,
        "name": "MindWanderer",
        "username": "MindWanderer",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-12-03T00:06:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Setback being a good guy is a \"fixed point?\" &nbsp;That would explain the effect of the Spite drugs on him. &nbsp;Him as the protagonist of that whole storyline would be a lot of fun.</p><p>Haka's mana going out of control would be a pretty great idea. &nbsp;Maybe at first he accidentally killed someone in self-defense, but holding onto a captured soul and not striking back out with it started to drain him psychologically. &nbsp;At first he became more violent but refused to use the mana for violence, then realized that holding onto it increased his strength and chose not to. &nbsp;Mechanically, he could be like Chokepoint--he could even have \"hero\" targets in his own deck, and grow stronger as he destroys them, environment targets, and anything else he can get his hands on.</p><p>I can easily see Unity ask just plain selfish, which is pretty close to evil. &nbsp;She might even delight in watching her creations kill people, just because she's so proud of them. &nbsp;That would be less her \"becoming\" evil, more her lacking a moral center to begin with.</p><p>But I can also see her becoming evil due to rejection. &nbsp;She desperately wants to be accepted. &nbsp;What if Tachyon refused her into the F5 because her \"audition\" robot turned out too violent? &nbsp;She could become a supervillain just because she felt she had something to prove. &nbsp;Maybe not a \"conquer/destroy the world\" sort of villain, but maybe an Iron Legacy sort, who does evil things with good(-ish) intentions.</p><p>There's also Golem Unity, who has a clear \"corrupted AI\" path to becoming evil. &nbsp;Maybe she wasn't copied over correctly and just comes out evil, or maybe she just ends up on one of the paths above.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:11:08.620Z",
