        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/jeysie/{size}/1868_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-12-03T16:06:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Ironically if you'd been right, it would have been a pretty tidy explanation for why Setback's niceness is a fixed point. Namely that the compounds work like Super Serum in the Marvel universe.</p><p>So use the compounds on a serial killer and you get a hate-crazed super-strong and powerful bloodthirsty obsessed serial killer.</p><p>And use the compounds on a somewhat ditzy nice guy and you get a really sweet incredibly nice guy with a peak physique who has Ditzy Luck Powers.</p><p>Of course this kind of also implies that Spite being a scary mass murdering SOB is also a fixed point, so, uh, maybe this not being the case is for the best.</p>",
        "post_number": 26,
